IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `ta-nouns`
IMPORT `ta-interpretation`

-- Tests of s 14.  Expected values are written from the text (the quoted words beside each), not from the rules' output.
-- Positional OF, with the columns named once:
--   Proceeds facts:   the proceeds itself, represents them, a payment or reward in connection with the act
--   Property facts:   likely to be used, applied for a proscribed organisation, proceeds of terrorism acts, proceeds of acts carried out for terrorism

`no proceeds fact` MEANS `Proceeds facts` OF FALSE, FALSE, FALSE
`the proceeds itself` MEANS `Proceeds facts` OF TRUE, FALSE, FALSE
`only represents the proceeds indirectly` MEANS `Proceeds facts` OF FALSE, TRUE, FALSE
`only a reward in connection with the act` MEANS `Proceeds facts` OF FALSE, FALSE, TRUE

-- s 14(2)(a) "includes ... represents the proceeds ... (including payments or other rewards in connection with its commission)"
#ASSERT `s 14(2)(a) the property is proceeds of the act` `the proceeds itself` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 14(2)(a) the property is proceeds of the act` `only represents the proceeds indirectly` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 14(2)(a) the property is proceeds of the act` `only a reward in connection with the act` EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- a list that "includes" is not closed: with none of the three facts the text does not answer
#ASSERT `s 14(2)(a) the property is proceeds of the act` `no proceeds fact` EQUALS NOTHING

-- s 14(2)(b) "includes ... applied or made available, or is to be applied or made available, for use by the organisation"
#ASSERT `s 14(2)(b) the property is among the organisation's resources` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 14(2)(b) the property is among the organisation's resources` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

`property likely to be used` MEANS `Property facts` OF TRUE, FALSE, `no proceeds fact`, `no proceeds fact`
`property of a proscribed organisation only` MEANS `Property facts` OF FALSE, TRUE, `no proceeds fact`, `no proceeds fact`
`proceeds of an act of terrorism only` MEANS `Property facts` OF FALSE, FALSE, `the proceeds itself`, `no proceeds fact`
`proceeds of an act carried out for terrorism only` MEANS `Property facts` OF FALSE, FALSE, `no proceeds fact`, `only represents the proceeds indirectly`
`property of no kind in s 14` MEANS `Property facts` OF FALSE, FALSE, `no proceeds fact`, `no proceeds fact`
`every kind of property in s 14` MEANS `Property facts` OF TRUE, TRUE, `the proceeds itself`, `the proceeds itself`

-- A property that meets no limb is outside what s 14 lists, and s 14(2) "includes": NOTHING, never JUST FALSE.
-- s 14(1)(a) "likely to be used for the purposes of terrorism (including any resources of a proscribed organisation)"
#ASSERT `s 14(1)(a) the property is likely to be used for the purposes of terrorism, or is a proscribed organisation's resources` `property likely to be used` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 14(1)(a) the property is likely to be used for the purposes of terrorism, or is a proscribed organisation's resources` `property of a proscribed organisation only` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 14(1)(a) the property is likely to be used for the purposes of terrorism, or is a proscribed organisation's resources` `proceeds of an act of terrorism only` EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 14(1)(b) "proceeds of the commission of acts of terrorism"
#ASSERT `s 14(1)(b) the property is proceeds of the commission of acts of terrorism` `proceeds of an act of terrorism only` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 14(1)(b) the property is proceeds of the commission of acts of terrorism` `proceeds of an act carried out for terrorism only` EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 14(1)(c) "proceeds of acts carried out for the purposes of terrorism"; s 14(2)(a) carries "represents" into the limb
#ASSERT `s 14(1)(c) the property is proceeds of acts carried out for the purposes of terrorism` `proceeds of an act carried out for terrorism only` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 14(1)(c) the property is proceeds of acts carried out for the purposes of terrorism` `proceeds of an act of terrorism only` EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 14(1) "means" the three limbs and nothing else
#ASSERT `s 14(1) the property is terrorist property` `property likely to be used` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 14(1) the property is terrorist property` `property of a proscribed organisation only` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 14(1) the property is terrorist property` `proceeds of an act of terrorism only` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 14(1) the property is terrorist property` `proceeds of an act carried out for terrorism only` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 14(1) the property is terrorist property` `every kind of property in s 14` EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- "means" closes the definition (fork F1, reading (a)): property of no kind in s 14 is outside it
#ASSERT `s 14(1) the property is terrorist property` `property of no kind in s 14` EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- 19 assertions written; 19 satisfied (run with l4 1.6.109 on the main build; check.sh recounts)
